ame>Blaustein</surname><given-names>JD</given-names></name><name><surname>Erskine</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Feminine sexual behavior: cellular integration of hormonal and afferent information in the rodent forebrain.</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Pfaff</surname><given-names>DW</given-names></name><name><surname>Arnold</surname><given-names>AP</given-names></name><name><surname>Etgen</surname><given-names>AM</given-names></name><name><surname>Fahrbach</surname><given-names>SE</given-names></name><name><surname>Rubin</surname><given-names>RT</given-names></name></person-group><source>Hormones, Brain and Behavior</source><publisher-loc>New York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Academic Press</publisher-name><fpage>139</fpage><lpage>191</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002210-Erskine1"><label>22</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Erskine</surname><given-names>MS</given-names></name></person-group><year>1989</year><article-title>Solicitation behavior in the estrous female rat: a review.</article-title><source>Horm Behav</source><volume>23</volume><fpage>473</fpage><lpage>502</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">2691387</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0002210-Champagne2"><label>23</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Champagne</surname><given-names>FA</given-names></name><name><surname>Weaver</surname><given-names>ICG</given-names></name><name><surname>Diorio</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Sharma</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Meaney</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Natural variations in maternal care are associated with estrogen receptor alpha expression and estrogen sensitivity in the medial preoptic area.</article-title><so